  "query_preview": "..Brief ridging will return over the weekend with \ngradual warming expected each day. Winds will remain out of the \nnortheast to east through this morning before starting to shift to \nthe southeast to south. Southerly winds will then continue through \nSunday, becoming gusty in the afternoon. A couple of shortwaves will \nmove through the mid-level flow, first one on Sunday and then a \nsecond one on Monday. Each wave will increase the mid-level moisture \nwith Sunday seeing an increase in cloud cover but it is lacking lift \nfor anything more than some isolated shower activity. As the \nmoisture and lift increase on Monday, we should see more isolated to \nscattered showers develop through the afternoon, mainly across the \nhigher terrain. \n\nThe midweek period looks like it will be overshadowed by a \ndeveloping low over the eastern Pacific. Models remain split on the \nexact trajectory of this low but what does look likely is that \ntemperatures will start to cool and winds will increase and become \ngusty out of the southwest. Chances for precipitation look to be \nfairly limited as the center of the low is slated to track to the \nnorth of the region. The flow then turns zonal for the end of the \nweek.",
